Every "Because you…" line (Picks' why line, list rows, the welcome tour, the
reveal line and its poster heading, the Taste Mixes anchor lane) says
"enjoyed", whatever the rating, on web and iPhone. /api/pick-why names loved
(4.5★+) films first among the four closest and keeps 4★ anchors when none is
loved (pickWhyAnchors). Web why cache bumped to montage_why:v2. Mix-name
parsing still reads cached "Because you loved X" names.

The shared rating verb's 4★ word is "enjoyed" (was "really liked"): rule
1603's rows and push ("Sam also enjoyed Heat"), the why line's prompt and
checks (a stored "really liked" still reads as 4★), the star read-backs
("enjoyed it") and the film sheet verdict ("You enjoyed this").

The notification switch is "Friends who enjoyed it too" on web and iPhone
Settings; detail and threshold unchanged. Invariant 1620 added; 220, 234,
458, 719, 1337, 1412, 1501, 1538, 1567, 1603 amended. Swift not compiled
here. [ds-log: n/a lib/taste-mixes.ts changes only a mix label's wording, no scoring or ranking]

